1. d4 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bh3 (3. Bg2 { Sound way to respond } 3... Bf5 4. Nf3) 3... Bxh3 4. Nxh3 c5 5. Be3 (5. dxc5 Nc6 6. O-O e5 7. Bg5 Bxc5 8. Bxf6 Qxf6 (8... gxf6 { Black can castle queeenside. }) 9. Qxd5 { Do not capture the bishop with the queen; it hangs the bishop }) 5... Nc6 6. c3 e6 7. dxc5 Ng4 8. Bg5 (8. Bd4 e5 (8... Nxd4 9. cxd4 { Capturing with the knight enables white to secure the pawn chain }) 9. Be3 { Playing E5 forces the Bishop back; this enables the capture of the bishop and doubling up of the pawns in front of the king } 9... Nxe3 10. fxe3 Bxc5) 8... f6 (8... Be7 { Be7 - you allow white the opportunity to cling to the pawn } 9. Bxe7 Qxe7 10. b4) 9. Bf4 Bxc5 10. b4 Bb6 11. b5 Nce5 12. Na3 O-O 13. O-O Rc8 14. Qd2 Qe8 15. Rac1 Qh5 16. Kg2 Bc5 17. Qb2 (17. Nc2 Nc4 18. Qd3 e5 { E5 dops D5 with the a check to the queen } (18... Bxf2 { Tactic to win } 19. Nxf2 (19. Rxf2 Qxh3+ 20. Kxh3 Nxf2+ 21. Kg2 Nxd3 22. exd3) 19... Qxh2+ 20. Kf3 Nge5+ 21. Bxe5 fxe5+ 22. Kg4 Rf5 23. Qxf5 exf5+ 24. Kf3 e4+ 25. Nxe4 dxe4+ 26. Kf4 Qh6+ 27. Kxf5 Qg6+ 28. Kf4 Rf8#) 19. Qxd5+ Kh8) 17... Bxa3 18. Qxa3 Nc4 19. Qxa7 e5 20. Qc5 (20. Be3 d4 21. cxd4 Ngxe3+ 22. fxe3 Nxe3+ 23. Kf2 Qxh3 24. Kxe3 Qh6+ 25. Kf3 Rxc1 26. Rxc1 Qxc1 27. Qc5 Qh1+ 28. Ke3 exd4+ 29. Kxd4 Rd8+ 30. Kc3 Qe1+ 31. Kb3 Qb1+ 32. Kc3 Kh8 33. Qc4 Re8 34. Kd2 b6 35. a3 Qg1 36. a4 Qxh2 37. Qd3 Qg1 38. Kc3 Qe1+ 39. Kc4 Qc1+ 40. Kb3 Qa1 41. g4 Qe5 42. e3 Qg3 43. Kc4 Qc7+ 44. Kb3 Qc1 45. e4 Qa1 46. Kc2 Qxa4+ 47. Kd2 Qa2+ 48. Ke3 Qg2 49. g5 fxg5 50. Qd5 Rf8 51. Kd4 Qf2+ 52. Kc4 Rc8+ 53. Qc6 Rd8 54. Qd5 Rxd5 55. exd5 Qc5+ 56. Kd3 Qxd5+ 57. Ke3 Qe5+ 58. Kd2 g4 59. Kd3 g3 60. Kc4 g2 61. Kb3 g1=Q 62. Kc2 Qf2+ 63. Kb3 Qfb2+ 64. Kc4 Qbxb5#) 20... Rxc5 21. b6 exf4 22. gxf4 Nce3+ 23. fxe3 Nxe3+ 24. Kf2 Qxh3 25. Rc2 Nxc2 26. Rc1 Qe3+ 27. Kg2 Qxc1 28. e3 Nxe3+ { White Resigns } *


