1. e4 c5 2. d4 e6 3. d5 d6 4. Nc3 Ne7 (4... Nf6 { Black should have developed the Knight to F6 - Black is playing to passively }) 5. Nf3 h6 (5... e5 { Black should have play E5 to close down white's advantage } 6. Nd2 { Knight to d6 is white's continuation to pave the way for pawn to f4 }) 6. Bb5+ Bd7 7. dxe6 Bxb5 8. exf7+ Kxf7 9. Nxb5 Qb6 (9... Qa5+ 10. Nc3) 10. Nxd6+ Kf6 11. e5+ Ke6 12. Ng5+ Kxe5 (12... hxg5 { Continuation to for the black queen and king if black h6 pawn captured the knight on g5 } 13. Qg4+ Kxe5 14. Nc4+) 13. O-O (13. Qe2+ Kd5 14. Qe4+ Kxd6 15. Qe6+ Kc7 16. Bf4+ Kd8 17. O-O-O+ Qd6 (17... Ke8 18. Qf7#) 18. Rxd6+ Nd7 19. Qxd7#) 13... Kf6 14. Re1 hxg5 15. Qf3+ Kg6 16. Re6+ Kh7 17. Qh5+ Kg8 18. Qf7+ Kh7 19. Bxg5 Ng8 20. Qg6# *


