1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 { Black's continuation of KF6 is the Caro Kann - Tartakower Variation } (4... Bf5) (4... Nd7) 5. f3 (5. Nxf6+ exf6 6. c3 Bd6 7. Bd3 O-O 8. Qc2 Re8+ 9. Ne2 h5) 5... Bf5 (5... Nxe4 { White Knight capturing the e4 pawn is another alternative line that black could have played } 6. fxe4 e5 7. dxe5 Qh4+) 6. Bc4 Nbd7 (6... Nxe4 { If black's knight had taken the e4 pawn, this is a possible continuation that white could have played } 7. fxe4 Bxe4 8. Nf3 e6 9. O-O Be7 10. Ne5 O-O 11. Nxf7 Rxf7 12. Bxe6) 7. Ng5 (7. Qe2 { Famous Trap } 7... h6 8. Nd6#) 7... e6 8. d5 (8. Ne2 { White should have played Knight to e2 and not d5 } 8... h6) 8... cxd5 9. Bb5 Qa5+ { Black Resigns } *


