1. e4 e5 2. d4 d6 3. Nf3 f6 4. Bc4 Nc6 5. c3 a5 6. a4 (6. Qb3 a4 7. Bf7+ Kd7 (7... Ke7 8. Qd5 Ra5) 8. Qe6#) 6... Nh6 7. Bxh6 gxh6 8. Nh4 (8. Nxe5 fxe5 (8... dxe5 { The problem with Knight capturing e5 pawn is that check mate is not guaranteed } 9. Qh5+ Kd7 (9... Ke7 10. Qf7+ Kd6) 10. Qf7+ Qe7 11. Qd5+ Qd6) 9. Qh5+ Ke7 (9... Kd7 10. Qf5+ Ke8 11. Qf7#) 10. Qf7#) (8. Ng5 { The problem the Knight to g5 there is simply no checkmate } 8... hxg5 9. Qh5+) 8... h5 (8... Qe7 { Black queen to E7 enables the d7 square to be vacated for the protection of the black king } 9. Qh5+ Kd8) 9. Qxh5+ Kd7 10. Nf5 Qe8 11. Bf7 Qd8 12. d5 Ne7 13. Be6# *


