1. e4 c6 2. Bc4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. Bb5+ Bd7 5. Nc3 Bxb5 6. Nxb5 Nc6 (6... e5 7. Nf3 Nc6 (7... e4 8. Nfd4 { Just pushing pawns gives up space for your opponents pieces }) 8. d4) 7. c3 a6 8. Nd4 Nxd4 9. cxd4 e6 10. Nf3 Bd6 11. d3 Ne7 12. O-O O-O 13. Re1 Qb6 14. a3 Nf5 15. b4 a5 { This would have been black's best optimal move } (15... Rfc8 { This would also have been a good alternative move }) 16. Bd2 (16. bxa5 Rxa5 { If white had taken the a5 pawn we would have created another weakness. Black also has a weakness : the A7 pawn; but beacause black's pieces are more active, black is in a better position to attack white's weakness. }) 16... axb4 17. axb4 Nxd4 { This has created a specific weakness - the knight attack the C4 pawn, an isolated pawn } (17... Ra6 18. Rxa6 Qxa6 { Alternative strategy 1 to control the A File - The Queen controls the A file after the capture. If he does not capture the rook and decides to move the white rook away from the a file, then black doubles up rooks onto the a file. }) 18. Rxa8 Rxa8 19. Nxd4 (19. Bc3 { Bishop to c3 would have been white's best move } 19... Nxf3+ { Knight to f3 would have been blacks best play in this situation } 20. Qxf3 Bxb4 21. Rb1 Bxc3 22. Rxb6 Ra1+ 23. Rb1 Rxb1+ 24. Qd1 Rxd1#) 19... Qxd4 20. Qe2 Bxb4 (20... Ra2 { This would also have been an alternative workable strategy }) 21. Bxb4 Qxb4 22. g3 Qc3 23. Kg2 b5 (23... Ra1 { Trading the black rook for the white rook, gives scope for the white queen to attack and capture the b7 pawn. } 24. Rxa1 Qxa1 25. Qc2 g6 (25... Qa8 { Black queen to a8 is black's best move to protect the pawn on b7. } 26. Qc7 { White's best reply is queen to C7. This position is very difficult to win for white. } 26... h6 27. Qd7 Qb8 28. Qa4 b5 29. Qb4 Qb6 30. h4 Qa6 31. Qe7) 26. Qc8+ Kg7 27. Qxb7 { This is position is very hard to win. }) 24. Rb1 b4 25. Qb2 Qxb2 26. Rxb2 Rb8 27. Kf3 Kf8 28. d4 b3 29. Ke3 Ke7 30. Kd3 Kd6 (30... Kf6 { King f6 is also a fine alternative }) 31. Kc3 f6 (31... e5 32. dxe5+ Kxe5 33. Rxb3 (33. Re2+ Kd6 34. Kb2) 33... Rxb3+ 34. Kxb3) 32. f4 (32. Re2 b2 33. Rxb2 Rxb2 34. Kxb2) 32... Rb7 { This is a waiting move. } (32... e5 33. dxe5+ fxe5 34. fxe5+ Kxe5 35. Re2+) 33. h4 (33. Kd3 e5 34. dxe5+ fxe5 35. fxe5+ Kxe5 36. Re2+ Kd6 37. Rb2) 33... h5 34. Rxb3 (34. Rb1 b2 35. Rxb2) 34... Rxb3+ 35. Kxb3 e5 36. fxe5+ fxe5 37. dxe5+ Kxe5 38. Kc3 Ke4 39. Kd2 Kf3 40. Kd3 Kxg3 41. Kd4 Kxh4 42. Kxd5 Kg3 43. Ke4 h4 44. Ke3 h3 45. Ke2 h2 46. Kf1 h1=Q+ 47. Ke2 Qf3+ 48. Kd2 Kf4 49. Ke1 Qg2 50. Kd1 Ke3 51. Kc1 Kd3 52. Kd1 Qd2# *


