1. e4 e5 2. d4 Nc6 3. dxe5 (3. Nf3!! { Knight to f3 transposes to the Scotch }) (3. d5 { D5 is not bad but leads to closed positions }) 3... Nxe5 4. Nc3 Nf6 { Playing KF3 is a big mistake } 5. f4 Nc6 6. e5 Ng8 7. Nf3 d6 8. Bb5 Bd7 (8... dxe5 { The drawback of this move is that whit might be cashing in too soon as the bishop is given up too soon. } 9. Qxd8+ (9. fxe5 { Taking with the pawn is advisable as white has huge initiative }) 9... Kxd8 10. Bxc6 bxc6 11. Nxe5) 9. O-O dxe5 10. fxe5 Qe7 (10... Bc5+ 11. Kh1 Nge7 12. Ng5 { This line would have been blacks best response but it does not really help }) 11. Nd5 Qc5+ 12. Be3 Nd4 13. Bxd7+ Kxd7 14. Nc3 Rd8 15. Bxd4 Qc6 16. e6+ fxe6 (16... Qxe6 17. Ne5+ (17. Bf6+ { Bishop to f6 is a better move } 17... Kc8 18. Qxd8#) 17... Kc8 18. Nxf7) 17. Ne5+ Kc8 18. Nxc6 bxc6 19. Rxf8 Rxf8 20. Bxg7 Rd8 21. Qg4 Nh6 22. Qxe6+ Kb7 23. Bxh8 Rxh8 *


